WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.682
(gentle music)

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.460
^- Hi my name is Harmony Dust Grillo,

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.910
^and I used to be a stripper.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.440
So I was raised in a very violent neighborhood

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.710
and a chaotic home.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.100
Just as an example, Domino's Pizza

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.003
would not deliver to us after dark,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.130
and even the police wouldn't come

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.340
to our neighborhood after dark.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.280
I remember being eight years old

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.620
and someone coming into our home and beating my mother

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.460
nearly to death with brass knuckles.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.943
It wasn't until three days later

00:00:31.943 --> 00:00:33.763
that the police finally came.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.800
She called them but they didn't show up

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.970
and she actually, before she lost consciousness

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.780
called a friend who ended up

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.130
taking her to the hospital and saving her life.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.230
I can still remember sitting in the living room

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.260
when the police finally showed up and knocked on the door

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.750
and said that they got a call that there was a disturbance.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.490
So that's kind of the context that I grew up in.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.810
My household was really chaotic

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:57.330
because my mother struggled with drug addiction,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.870
and that meant that I was exposed to a lot

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.770
including sexual abuse from a very early age,

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:07.150
starting at the age of five, and then I was raped as a teen.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.300
One of my abusers was my mother's boyfriend.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.620
At that point I was 13,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.870
and I finally started standing up for myself.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:15.963
I ran away from home.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.110
My mom realized that I was serious

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.120
and that I wasn't coming back until he was gone,

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.343
so she finally kicked him out.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.050
I came home, only she left with him.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.170
She ended up leaving with him

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.850
and so she left me at 13

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.560
with my eight year old brother for three months,

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.453
with $20 and a book of food stamps.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.030
Obviously $20 didn't last very long.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.550
The food stamps didn't last very long,

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.700
so I started stealing from the liquor store

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.110
to feed my brother and I,

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:46.560
and it was that summer that I became involved

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.410
with an older boy in my neighborhood.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.290
Because of the situation I was in,

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.930
I just saw a knight in shining armor.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.080
You know, when he was around I didn't have to steal

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.230
because he would buy my brother and I food.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.030
When he was around I felt protected

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.760
in that neighborhood that I lived in

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.570
because he would always tell me, I got your back.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.610
I'll take care of you.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.383
And so I became really, really attached to him.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.380
I ended up in a seven year long relationship with him

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.713
that ultimately became physically and emotionally abusive,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.053
and led me to working in the sex industry as a stripper,

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.920
and my boyfriend became my pimp.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.370
So every night I came home and gave him all of my money,

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:26.053
and he completely controlled my entire life.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.300
I was so broken just from years of abuse and low self-esteem

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.793
that I let him control my life.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.120
Afraid to leave him, didn't see a way out,

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.560
felt completely trapped in that situation.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.260
The thing about the sex industry

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.240
is that those of us that are in it,

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.103
most of us we end up using a stage name,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.300
and with that also creating

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.740
an entire alter identity that we hide behind,

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.300
and so I remember the first night I showed up

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.913
for my very first shift and the DJ said,

00:02:57.347 --> 00:02:58.327
"What do you want to go by?

00:02:58.327 --> 00:02:59.397
"What's your name?"

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.763
And I had only thought of it, so I said,

00:03:01.837 --> 00:03:03.730
"Harmony, that's my name."

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.400
And I remember watching him write Harmony

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.840
in black dry erase on the whiteboard

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.760
and it was just, it was too much.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.687
So I said, "No, no, no take it down.

00:03:14.687 --> 00:03:16.140
"I'll be Monique."

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.090
And really from that night forward

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.123
for the next few years, I became Monique.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.223
Monique was a compilation of other people's fantasies.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.740
Monique wasn't a real person.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.410
She was someone that I could hide behind

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:31.410
while I was working in the sex industry.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.280
Not only was my name fake,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.380
but everything I told the customers was fake.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.830
Everything about the life that I created

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.520
for Monique was a complete lie.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.440
It made me feel safe and it was the only way for me

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.840
that I could work as a stripper,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.710
but at the same time eventually

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.513
I began to lose sight of who Harmony was.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.060
The only people I had contact with were my abusive exploiter

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.643
and other women in the club, and the customers.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.400
No one really knew who I really was,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.700
and honestly I didn't know who I really was.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.640
You know, a lot of people think the sex industry

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.450
is so glamorous and so empowering, but it's hard.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.540
I don't think a lot of people see the reality

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.080
of what women working in the sex industry

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.990
have to deal with on a day to day basis.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:24.453
There's a lot of talk nowadays about sex trafficking,

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.710
and we're hearing all these stories about sex trafficking

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.730
and that it's happening here in the United States,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.230
but what I don't think everyone realizes

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.550
is that 70% of female trafficking victims

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.413
are trafficked into the commercial sex industry.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.420
That means they're working in strip clubs.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.920
They're working on porn sets.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.903
They're working for escort agencies.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.760
They're working in every single area of the commercial

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.710
sex industry, that's where they're working.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.605
We can't turn a blind eye to that,

00:04:51.605 --> 00:04:54.363
and I think that's super important for people to know.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:55.550
We get called names,

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:58.310
and touched when we don't want to be touched,

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.230
and you know I remember there were several occasions

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.843
where a customer would violate me,

00:05:04.843 --> 00:05:07.633
assault me, sexually assault me,

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.290
and you know I would (laughs) actually I was so angry,

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:13.480
I would just take off my stiletto

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.920
and I would literally beat them in the head with it,

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.660
and I felt so powerless.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.340
From my perspective it was self-defense

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.860
but they would look at me and see a woman

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.470
working in a strip club that's half naked

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:25.050
and think basically that I was asking for it,

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.270
and so working there was really hard.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:29.370
Ultimately what got me out of that,

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.823
it began with a friendship,

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.620
and just a person who loved me unconditionally

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:36.140
and didn't judge me for the crazy life

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.313
that I was living, just loved me.

00:05:38.387 --> 00:05:41.550
It was through that friendship that I saw an example

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.730
of a woman who had boundaries.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:44.700
She really inspired me,

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.580
so eventually I started going to church,

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.270
and I started just pursuing a relationship with God.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:53.140
My heart started changing, my mind started changing,

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:57.480
and I started to believe that I'm lovable

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.450
and that I have value,

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.560
and that maybe I was even put on this earth

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.128
for a purpose that was beyond

00:06:04.128 --> 00:06:06.970
working in the sex industry as a stripper

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.120
and being stuck in an abusive relationship.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:14.310
I finally got the courage to leave the ex-boyfriend/pimp

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.810
and leave the sex industry,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.560
and start on this recovery journey,

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.740
this healing journey that completely changed my life.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:25.400
I remember a few years after that,

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.200
I found myself sitting across the street

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.250
from the strip club where I used to work,

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:33.220
and I felt like I was sitting outside of a prison

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.813
that had once held me captive.

00:06:35.146 --> 00:06:38.390
I knew that there were other women who worked there

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:41.050
who maybe still felt as trapped as I once did,

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.810
and I wanted to do something to support them.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.760
So I didn't know what to do,

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.280
and I just started writing hand written notes on postcards

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.430
and put them on their cars and just let them know,

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.170
like hey, I've been through maybe some things

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.833
similar to what you've been through and I'm here for you.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.370
It was from that moment

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.133
that the vision of Treasures was birthed.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.080
I ended up starting

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.690
a nonprofit organization called Treasures,

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:08.480
and we are an outreach and support group for women

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:09.920
in the commercial sex industry

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.470
and victims of sexual exploitation and trafficking.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:15.740
We reach women with the simple message that changed my life,

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.093
and that message is that they are loved,

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.810
and valued, and purposed, and that support is available

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.660
for them if and when they want it,

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:24.960
if and when they're ready,

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.060
and that we're willing to just show up

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.030
and love them unconditionally

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:32.963
and walk with them through their process and their journey.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:35.330
Stripping changed my life.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:38.720
I was already a super broken girl going into it,

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.393
and whatever sense of identity that I had left,

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:46.070
I felt like stripping stripped away from me.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.730
I didn't think I would live to see 21.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.110
I thought if someone else didn't take me out,

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:54.340
I was gonna take my own life 'cause I was that hopeless,

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.456
and at the same time you know,

00:07:56.456 --> 00:07:59.750
now I wouldn't be doing what I'm doing

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.340
if it weren't for stripping,

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.330
and if it weren't for everything that I went through.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.330
What I really hope in sharing my story

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:08.420
and sharing everything that I've shared today

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.320
is that people will see the humanity

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:14.053
in the woman on the other end of the dollar,

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:18.550
and that behind every image that you see

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:22.763
of a woman in a strip club, in porn,

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.513
is a real person with a real story.

00:08:25.568 --> 00:08:28.151
(gentle music)

